<p>Israel and Lebanon agreed to extend the April 16 cessation of hostilities by 45 days after two days of U.S.-mediated talks in Washington, the U.S. State Department said Friday. State Department spokesman Tommy Pigott said the extension would allow talks to continue, with political negotiations scheduled for June 2-3 and a separate security track involving military delegations set to begin at the Pentagon on May 29. President Trump announced the ceasefire on April 16, and it had been due to expire Sunday, but Israel and Hezbollah have continued to exchange fire since it took effect. Violence continued as the Washington talks concluded: Israel issued evacuation warnings for parts of Tyre before strikes it said targeted Hezbollah infrastructure, and Lebanon&#x27;s health ministry said at least 37 people were wounded, including hospital workers, women and children. Israel said its latest operations were not covered by the ceasefire arrangement because Hezbollah was not part of the diplomatic process.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/aDoX170AWh3-ru8mvrr4c1crgvEnHwqSsXYTaRo8qoAMcrTiFAzQbpvzL2Rq3sp7P8ivXgFZ6zx-GEjsnhnPO3wpQ8IgsbbTkKmKZjV-yPorMtA0cNaZFeieI_i1qOZCc7HH2hmZ6pdMlVkTKTzicAE' alt='Delegations from Israel and Lebanon agreed to hold another round of negotiations on June 2-3.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Negotiating gap: Le Temps reported that Lebanon sought a permanent and definitive ceasefire before any continued negotiations on a possible security agreement, while Israel demanded Hezbollah&#x27;s disarmament.</li><li>Hezbollah posture: Hezbollah has publicly opposed direct talks between Lebanon and Israeli officials, while sources cited by Pravda said the group indirectly conveyed readiness for a direct ceasefire if Israel agreed.</li></ul><blockquote>We hope these discussions will advance lasting peace between the two countries, full recognition of each other&#x27;s sovereignty and territorial integrity, and establishing genuine security along their shared border - Tommy Pigott</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Lebanese negotiating delegation: The delegation said the extension would provide &quot;critical breathing space&quot; for Lebanese citizens, reinforce state institutions and support a political path toward stability. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/05/15/lebanon-says-truce-extension-with-israel-and-us-backed-security-create-opportunity-for-lasting-stability_6753500_4.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li><li>Israeli Ambassador Yechiel Leiter: Leiter called the Washington discussions frank and constructive and said there would be ups and downs in the process. (<a href='https://www.newsis.com/view/NISX20260516_0003632127'>Newsis</a>)</li><li>Lebanese government position: Lebanon demanded an end to Israeli attacks and to what it described as the occupation of Lebanese territory during the Washington talks. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/5/15/lebanon-talks-israel-attack'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/israel-lebanon-agree-to-extension-of-ceasefire-says-us/article70984881.ece'>Israel, Lebanon agree to 45-day extension of ceasefire, says U.S.</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cqlpzzl0d67o'>Israel and Lebanon agree to extend ceasefire, US state department says</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://japantoday.com/category/world/israel-lebanon-extend-ceasefire-by-45-days-as-washington-talks-conclude'>Israel, Lebanon extend ceasefire by 45 days as Washington talks conclude</a> - japantoday.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/middle-east-israel-lebanon-agree-to-extend-truce-us-says/live-77167235'>Middle East: Israel, Lebanon agree to extend truce, US says</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/05/israel-lebanon-say-extending-ceasefire-despite-new-strikes'>Israel, Lebanon say extending ceasefire despite new strikes</a> - al-m